    "description": "Developing, maintaining, and deploying iOS application which uses Mobile and Third-party frameworks, which \r\nare not limited to, Camera, Geolocation, SQLite. Consumption of WebAPI and parsing of data for iOS application.\n\nInvolved in all the phases of software development life cycle of the project.\n\nDeveloping web applications using Microsoft .Net frameworks, Microsoft SQL server\n\nUsing Windows Authentication from ASP.NET membership provider to authenticate user credentials\n\nCreating business logic layer using C#, VB and ASP.NET MVC\n\nDesigning Responsive UI using Razor syntax, HTML5, CSS, JavaScript, jQuery, AJAX, Bootstrap, Telerik UI for ASP.Net MVC, Kendo UI for ASP.Net MVC, Datatables and third party libraries.\n\nUsing Google Maps to retrieve real time data from ArcGIS web service\n\nDeveloping data access layer using Entity Framework \n\nCreating and consuming WCF services, Web APIs and web services (Edmunds, USPS, ArcGIS, NHTSA)\n\nCreating tables, view, user defined types, stored procedures, scalar and table valued functions, views and triggers to store, manipulate and fetch data from  SQL databases\n\nMigrated data from different data sources to SQL server\n\nUsing Linked Server to gather data from different SQL servers to generate visual reports\n\nUsing RedGate Toolbelt, SQL Profiler for performance tuning and database deployment\n\nUtilizing LINQ to query and retrieve data from different data source (SQL, Objects, XML and DataSet)\n\nUsing WinSCP SFTP client to transfer and receive files weekly among other agencies\n\nCreated a windows service to process files located at a specified location\n\nImplementing MSMQ to run Ad hoc processes\n\nUsing TFS for version control and deploying applications to server\n\nIntegrating HuntFishPA data into Agency’s applications\n\nWorking with client to gather business requirement and functional specifications\n\nUsing ELMAH for error logging",
